{"title":"NTA Abhyas (NEET)","category":"Medical","bank":"nta_abhyas_neet","subject":"Physics","chapter":"Experimental Physics","count":16,"questions":[{"id":102203,"subject":"Physics","chapter":"Experimental Physics","exam":"Medical","examName":"NTA Abhyas (NEET)","q":"<p>There is an unknown quantity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mfrac><mi>l</mi><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>, here <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi></math> is length <math>\r <mo stretchy='false'>(</mo>\r</math>in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cm</mi></math><math>\r <mo stretchy='false'>)</mo>\r</math> measured using a scale having least count of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1 </mn><mi>cm</mi></math>. and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo> </mo></math>is a quantity known accurately. Find the percentage error in measurement of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> for <math>\r <mrow>\r  <mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mo> </mo><mtext>cm</mtext></mrow>\r</math>?</p>","options":["<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1 </mn><mo>%</mo></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6 </mn><mo>%</mo></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2 </mn><mo>%</mo></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4 </mn><mo>%</mo></math>"],"answer":3,"solution":"<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mfrac><mi>ℓ</mi><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>ℓ</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>Δ</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>Δ</mi><mi>ℓ</mi></mrow><mi>ℓ</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>Δ</mi><mi>ℓ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>ℓ</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math x