<math> <mrow> <mo>=</mo> <mo>+</mo> <mn>5</mn> <mo>×</mo> <mtext>0.01</mtext> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>=</mo> <mo>+</mo> <mtext>0.05 mm</mtext> </mrow> </math><br /><br />so actual diameter<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>=</mo> <mtext>d</mtext> <mo>-</mo> <mtext>0.05</mtext> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>=</mo> <mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace> <mtext>1.20 mm</mtext> </mrow> </math>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"NTA Abhyas (NEET) 2020","_marksId":"615454d714bf43750e14acb9","questionType":"singleCorrect","type":"singleCorrect","_repairLog":["medical_cache_enrich"]},{"id":102205,"subject":"Physics","chapter":"Experimental Physics","exam":"Medical","examName":"NTA Abhyas (NEET)","q":"The length of a wire of a potentiometer is <math><mn>100</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> and the emf of its standard cell is <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></math> volt. It is employed to measured emf of a battery whose internal resistance is <math><mn>0.5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>. If the balance point is obtained at <math><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"script\"> </mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"script\"> </mi><mn>30</mn></math> cm from the positive end, the emf of the battery is -","options":["<math><mn>0.2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></math>","<math><mn>0.3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></math>","<math><mn>0.4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></math>","<math><mn>0.5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></math>"],"answer":1,"solution":"<math><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>l</mi></math></br></br><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ε</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ε</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mo>∴</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ε</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mn>30</mn></math><br /><br /><math><mo>∴</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ε</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mn>0.3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></math></br></br>l = balance length</br></br>L = length of potentialmeter wire","difficulty":"Medium","source":"NTA Abhyas (NEET) 2020","_marksId":"615454d7bdf4569e574d5ee3","questionType":"singleCorrect","type":"singleCorrect","_repairLog":["medical_cache_enrich"]},{"id":102206,"subject":"Physics","chapter":"Experimental Physics","exam":"Medical","examName":"NTA Abhyas (NEET)","q":"A galvanometer, with a scale divided into <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>150</mn></math> equal divisions, has current sensitivity of <math><mn>10</mn></math> divisions per milliampere and voltage sensitivity of <math><mn>2</mn></math> divisions per millivolt. Find shunt resistance for making an ammeter of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>.","options":["<math><mn>1.25</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mo>×</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>–</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>","<math><mn>12.5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mo>×</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>–</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>","<math><mn>125</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mo>×</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>–</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>","<math><mn>0.125</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mo>×</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>–</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>"],"answer":1,"solution":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"\" close=\"}\" separators=\"|\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi>mA</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>75</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi>mV</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced><mo>⇒</mo><mo> </mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>–</mo><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>12.5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mo>×</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>–</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"NTA Abhyas (NEET) 2020","_marksId":"615454d75fef30dd6edf22c5","questionType":"singleCorrect","type":"singleCorrect","_repairLog":["medical_cache_enrich"]},{"id":102207,"subject":"Physics","chapter":"Experimental Physics","exam":"Medical","examName":"NTA Abhyas (NEET)","q":"Two tangent galvanometers having coils of the same radius are connected in series. A current flowing in them produces deflections of <math><mn>60</mn><mo>°</mo></math> and <math><mn>45</mn><mo>°</mo></math> respectively. The ratio of the number of turns in the coil is -","options":["<math><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></math>","<math><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></math>","<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>–</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>","<math> <mrow> <msqrt> <mn>3</mn> </msqrt></mrow></math>"],"answer":3,"solution":"In series, current is same in tangent galvanometer.<br /><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi><mo>⇒</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mi>ni</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∵</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></math> is same<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>∝</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi><mo>⇒</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>60</mn><mo>°</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>45</mn><mo>°</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>1</mn></mfrac></math>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"NTA Abhyas (NEET) 2020","_marksId":"615454d735fe59e1dad8eb3a","questionType":"singleCorrect","type":"singleCorrect","_repairLog":["medical_cache_enrich"]},{"id":102208,"subject":"Physics","chapter":"Experimental Physics","exam":"Medical","examName":"NTA Abhyas (NEET)","q":"The coil of a moving coil galvanometer is wound over a metal frame in order to","options":["reduce hysteresis","provide electromagnetic damping","increase the moment of inertia","increase the sensitivity"],"answer":1,"solution":"The coil of a moving coil galvanometer is wound over a metal frame in order to provide electromagnetic damping by which the galvanometer becomes dead beat.","difficulty":"Medium","source":"NTA Abhyas (NEET) 2020","_marksId":"615454d733d60a09048660aa","questionType":"singleCorrect","type":"singleCorrect","_repairLog":["medical_cache_enrich"]},{"id":102209,"subject":"Physics","chapter":"Experimental Physics","exam":"Medical","examName":"NTA Abhyas (NEET)","q":"The deflection in a moving coil galvanometer is","options":["directly proportional to the torsional constant","directly proportional to the number of turns in the coil","inversely proportional to the area of the coil","inversely proportional to the current flowing"],"answer":1,"solution":"Deflection is directly proportion